<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman Public Debt Administration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1881</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman Public Debt Administration was an organisation established in 1881 after the Ottoman state defaulted on its foreign loans. Run by representatives of European creditors, it collected certain state revenues directly to service the debt. It placed much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>'s finances under foreign supervision, a marker of its loss of fiscal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</p></div>
